WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.462 --> 00:00:01.530
Blame feels good.

2
00:00:02.173 --> 00:00:03.027
For about a minute.

3
00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:07.070
I noticed that the leader we were studying
doesn't blame anybody.

4
00:00:07.866 --> 00:00:08.672
Not people.

5
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:10.753
Not circumstances.

6
00:00:11.676 --> 00:00:14.495
If you keep blaming
outside things, I said,

7
00:00:15.425 --> 00:00:16.555
you have an inside problem.

8
00:00:17.285 --> 00:00:18.984
The question strong leaders ask:

9
00:00:19.805 --> 00:00:21.489
Where did my process break down?

10
00:00:22.096 --> 00:00:23.694
Blame hands your power away.

11
00:00:24.594 --> 00:00:26.611
Auditing your process gets it back.

12
00:00:27.658 --> 00:00:30.271
In a small company it starts at the top.

13
00:00:31.051 --> 00:00:33.913
The leader takes accountability,
and then everyone does.

14
00:00:35.025 --> 00:00:36.153
Focus on the problem.

15
00:00:37.057 --> 00:00:37.725
What are my options?

16
00:00:38.563 --> 00:00:40.130
When have I been here before?

17
00:00:41.198 --> 00:00:42.556
Write something that went wrong.

18
00:00:43.337 --> 00:00:44.935
Write who you were tempted to blame.

